
  riscvsim › demo 6 · Wide values · RV64
  RV64 registers hold 64 bits; see what addw keeps.

   1  # RV64 registers hold 64 bits; build 0x0000_0100_0000_0005
   2  addi x1, x0, 1     # x1 = 1
   3  slli x1, x1, 40    # x1 = 1 << 40
   4  addi x2, x1, 5     # x2 = 0x0000_0100_0000_0005
   5  addw x3, x2, x0    # addw keeps the low 32 bits: 5
   6  addi x4, x0, -1    # -1 sets all 64 bits

  cycle 1
    IF addi x1, x0, 1  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › The first instruction, addi, is fetched from memory.

  cycle 2
    IF slli x1, x1, 40  ID addi x1, x0, 1  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 3
    IF addi x2, x1, 5  ID slli x1, x1, 40  EX addi x1, x0, 1  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 4
    IF addw x3,x2,x0  ID addi x2,x1,5  EX slli x1,x1…  MEM addi x1,x0,1  WB ·
    › slli needs x1 from addi, so it is forwarded from the EX/MEM latch and
      nobody waits.

  cycle 5
    IF addi x4,x0…  ID addw x3,x2…  EX addi x2,x1…  MEM slli x1…  WB addi x1…
    ✓ x1 = 1
    › addi needs x1 from slli, so it is forwarded from the EX/MEM latch and
      nobody waits.

  cycle 6
    IF ·  ID addi x4,x0,-1  EX addw x3,x2,x0  MEM addi x2,x1,5  WB slli x1,x1…
    ✓ x1 = 0x0000_0100_0000_0000
    › addw needs x2 from addi, so it is forwarded from the EX/MEM latch and
      nobody waits.

  cycle 7
    IF ·  ID ·  EX addi x4, x0, -1  MEM addw x3, x2, x0  WB addi x2, x1, 5
    ✓ x2 = 0x0000_0100_0000_0005
    › addi finishes and writes x2 = 0x0000_0100_0000_0005.

  cycle 8
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM addi x4, x0, -1  WB addw x3, x2, x0
    ✓ x3 = 5
    › addw finishes and writes x3 = 5.

  cycle 9
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB addi x4, x0, -1
    ✓ x4 = -1
    ✓ addi writes x4 = -1, and the program is finished.

  ✓ 9 cycles · 5 instructions · CPI 1.80 · 0 stalls · 0 mispredictions
    Ends with x1 = 0x0000_0100_0000_0000 · x2 = 0x0000_0100_0000_0005
              x3 = 5 · x4 = -1 (0xffff_ffff_ffff_ffff)
    No stalls: forwarding kept every instruction moving.

  ✓ You finished all six lessons.
